WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:06.980
Hi, it's sales. Our reps struggle to plan
their visits, and we're fewer people now.

2
00:00:06.980 --> 00:00:09.159
Can you make them more efficient?

3
00:00:09.509 --> 00:00:13.754
Let's find out today. I'll bring the two
product owners, and our agents.

4
00:00:15.754 --> 00:00:20.686
Who: our field sales reps. The pain:
planning visits with fewer people.

5
00:00:20.686 --> 00:00:24.159
The goal: more time with customers, for
every rep.

6
00:00:24.959 --> 00:00:29.609
The agents build a visit planner into the
field app we already run.

7
00:00:29.609 --> 00:00:32.594
Spec, build, review, tests. One agent
finds

8
00:00:32.594 --> 00:00:35.370
an issue; another fixes it, with a test.

9
00:00:44.220 --> 00:00:48.103
It's six in the evening, and my reps have
it on their phones.

10
00:00:50.903 --> 00:00:53.592
Now picture this in every product team,

11
00:00:53.592 --> 00:00:56.556
across the whole company, at the same
time.

12
00:01:03.856 --> 00:01:07.153
Delivery capacity is no longer the
bottleneck.

13
00:01:07.153 --> 00:01:10.235
Problem definition and company context
are.
